<title>SOUTH AFRICA: S.Africa govt financing 5.12 bln rand in November.</title>
<headline>S.Africa govt financing 5.12 bln rand in November.</headline>
<dateline>JOHANNESBURG 1996-11-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>Government financing amounted to 5.12 billion rand in November after it raised 3.37 billion rand in the bond markets and net short-term loans increased by 1.75 billion rand, the Department of Finance said on Wednesday.</p>
<p>This brought total financing for the financial year April to November to 32.92 billion rand, or 72.9 percent of total budgeted financing of 45.1 billion rand for the year.</p>
<p>(rand million)		Nov '96   April-Nov '96  Budgeted 96/97</p>
<p>Government bonds</p>
<p>and debentures	  3,667.8   28,434.1	 39,604.7</p>
<p>Short-term (net):</p>
<p>  Bridging bonds	     --   -2,980.5	 -3,616,5</p>
<p>  Tender bills	   -106.2    1,697.0	  3,616,5</p>
<p>  CPD		     1,853.5    2,934.4	  3,000.0</p>
<p>Foreign loans		  --    2,831.0	  2,500.0</p>
<p>Total financing	 5,115.1   32,916.0	 45,104.7</p>
<p>-- Johannesburg newsroom, +27 11 482-1003</p>
</text>
